WEBVTT

00:00:00.606 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.712 --> 00:00:06.328
In this lesson, we do a spa foot treatment, then a hand treatment with paraffin,

00:00:06.278 --> 00:00:07.070
step by step.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.030
No polish.

00:00:08.459 --> 00:00:11.659
The whole session usually takes about forty-five minutes to an hour,

00:00:11.609 --> 00:00:12.910
depending on the treatment.

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:14.590
Timing and products:

00:00:14.824 --> 00:00:17.710
follow your salon's treatment, and the brand's instructions.

00:00:18.357 --> 00:00:19.159
Step one:

00:00:19.332 --> 00:00:20.119
preparation.

00:00:20.527 --> 00:00:23.959
Wipe and disinfect the chair, the table and the footrest.

00:00:24.308 --> 00:00:25.959
Put a new liner in the foot bath.

00:00:26.307 --> 00:00:29.825
Metal foot tools must be sterilized, still sealed in their pouch,

00:00:29.775 --> 00:00:31.639
and opened in front of the client.

00:00:32.066 --> 00:00:34.439
Buffers and paper files are single use:

00:00:34.546 --> 00:00:36.199
a new set for every client.

00:00:36.781 --> 00:00:37.555
Step two:

00:00:37.894 --> 00:00:38.835
ask the client.

00:00:39.013 --> 00:00:43.235
Any diabetes, poor circulation, allergies, or wounds?

00:00:43.644 --> 00:00:44.355
Ask too:

00:00:44.543 --> 00:00:48.195
which scent she likes, and whether she would like to chat, or to rest.

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:53.235
Then run warm water into the lined tub, and test it with your own wrist:

00:00:53.421 --> 00:00:55.955
warm, comfortable, not hot.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:59.075
With a diabetic client, be extra careful.

00:00:59.747 --> 00:01:00.523
Step three:

00:01:00.855 --> 00:01:03.003
wash your hands, and put on gloves.

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:06.843
Look closely at the feet, the soles, and between the toes.

00:01:07.347 --> 00:01:12.603
Peeling or cracked skin between the toes, thick discolored nails, wounds:

00:01:12.952 --> 00:01:16.203
don't work on that area, and advise the client to see a doctor.

00:01:16.533 --> 00:01:19.723
If everything is fine, invite the client to put her feet in the tub.

00:01:20.062 --> 00:01:23.163
Soak for about five to ten minutes, depending on the treatment.

00:01:23.836 --> 00:01:24.694
Step four:

00:01:24.945 --> 00:01:25.974
exfoliation.

00:01:26.566 --> 00:01:28.934
Lift a foot out, and rest it on a towel.

00:01:29.276 --> 00:01:34.255
Rub the scrub in gentle circles, from the toes up to the top of the foot, the ankle,

00:01:34.205 --> 00:01:36.134
and more thoroughly on the heel.

00:01:36.477 --> 00:01:39.654
Fine grains only, like sugar or fine salt:

00:01:40.021 --> 00:01:42.854
big, sharp grains easily scratch the skin.

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:44.614
Avoid any broken skin.

00:01:44.875 --> 00:01:48.134
Then rinse in the tub, pat dry, and do the other foot.

00:01:48.806 --> 00:01:49.752
Step five:

00:01:49.924 --> 00:01:51.272
the skin around the nails.

00:01:51.592 --> 00:01:53.672
Dry the feet, between the toes too.

00:01:54.024 --> 00:01:57.183
Apply cuticle softener, wait as the brand instructs,

00:01:57.133 --> 00:01:59.992
then push back gently with a sterilized pusher.

00:02:00.402 --> 00:02:01.832
Don't cut the living skin.

00:02:02.181 --> 00:02:06.336
If the nails are long, cut them straight across, and file the corners lightly,

00:02:06.286 --> 00:02:08.072
as in the basic nail care lesson.

00:02:08.757 --> 00:02:09.610
Step six:

00:02:09.714 --> 00:02:10.490
the heels.

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:15.370
Use a foot file, gently and evenly, as instructed for that type of file.

00:02:15.718 --> 00:02:16.330
Feel it:

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:17.610
smooth is enough;

00:02:17.799 --> 00:02:19.850
there is no need to remove all the callus.

00:02:20.269 --> 00:02:24.570
File a few light strokes, feel the heel, and only file more if needed.

00:02:24.915 --> 00:02:26.730
File little, feel often.

00:02:26.993 --> 00:02:28.250
No callus shavers.

00:02:28.519 --> 00:02:31.610
If the client feels a burning sting, you have gone too far.

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:33.126
Step seven:

00:02:33.297 --> 00:02:34.326
foot massage.

00:02:34.567 --> 00:02:35.926
Apply massage cream.

00:02:36.105 --> 00:02:40.646
Long strokes from the toes up to the ankle, up the calf, toward the heart.

00:02:41.063 --> 00:02:45.686
Gentle thumb circles along the sole of the foot, then stroke each toe lightly.

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:48.166
Ask the client whether the pressure is right.

00:02:48.436 --> 00:02:50.326
Don't press on varicose veins.

00:02:50.511 --> 00:02:54.033
Finish each foot with a few long strokes, getting slower,

00:02:53.983 --> 00:02:56.166
then wrap the foot in a warm towel,

00:02:56.275 --> 00:02:57.686
so the client doesn't get cold.

00:02:58.272 --> 00:02:58.962
Step eight:

00:02:59.213 --> 00:03:04.028
if the treatment includes a foot mask, apply a layer, wrap it in thin film,

00:03:03.978 --> 00:03:05.362
then in a warm towel,

00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:08.002
for about ten minutes, as the brand instructs.

00:03:08.355 --> 00:03:09.602
The client relaxes.

00:03:09.774 --> 00:03:11.842
Meanwhile, you move on to the hands.

00:03:12.405 --> 00:03:13.288
Step nine:

00:03:13.395 --> 00:03:14.248
the hands.

00:03:14.487 --> 00:03:18.808
Soak the fingertips in a bowl of warm water for a few minutes, then dry them.

00:03:19.137 --> 00:03:23.608
Exfoliate more gently than on the feet, because the skin on the hands is thinner.

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:27.768
Then push back the skin around the nails gently, as with the feet.

00:03:28.369 --> 00:03:29.228
Step ten:

00:03:29.329 --> 00:03:30.348
hand massage.

00:03:30.794 --> 00:03:33.228
Take off your gloves, and wash your hands.

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:36.419
Both thumbs make long strokes over the back of the hand,

00:03:36.369 --> 00:03:38.268
from the knuckles toward the wrist.

00:03:38.602 --> 00:03:40.188
Gentle circles in the palm.

00:03:40.536 --> 00:03:43.548
Stroke along each finger, from the base to the tip.

00:03:43.954 --> 00:03:46.588
Moderate pressure, slow, and even.

00:03:46.928 --> 00:03:51.931
Finally, long strokes from the back of the hand up the forearm, a few times,

00:03:51.881 --> 00:03:52.908
getting slower.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:54.522
Step eleven:

00:03:54.704 --> 00:03:55.322
paraffin.

00:03:55.910 --> 00:03:59.802
Check the temperature as the brand instructs, then test it on your own wrist.

00:04:00.169 --> 00:04:01.962
Use it only on intact skin.

00:04:02.631 --> 00:04:04.842
Take the paraffin out into a separate bowl:

00:04:05.141 --> 00:04:07.722
never dip the client's hands into the shared pot.

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:11.322
Brush a few layers onto the back of the hand, and the palm.

00:04:11.824 --> 00:04:16.779
Wrap it in a thin bag, then put on cotton mitts, and leave it for about ten minutes,

00:04:16.729 --> 00:04:18.122
as the brand instructs.

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:20.122
If the client feels it is too hot:

00:04:20.372 --> 00:04:22.202
stop at once, and peel it off.

00:04:22.866 --> 00:04:23.732
Step twelve:

00:04:24.089 --> 00:04:27.092
remove the mitts, and peel off the paraffin in one go.

00:04:27.441 --> 00:04:29.092
Used paraffin is thrown away.

00:04:29.447 --> 00:04:31.732
Apply moisturizer, with light strokes.

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:36.372
Then unwrap the towel on the feet, wipe off the mask, and apply foot cream.

00:04:36.852 --> 00:04:39.492
Look over the skin on the hands and feet once more:

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:41.492
is anything red or stinging?

00:04:42.152 --> 00:04:43.176
Step thirteen:

00:04:43.443 --> 00:04:44.616
aftercare advice.

00:04:45.353 --> 00:04:48.696
Advise the client to moisturize her hands and feet every day.

00:04:49.127 --> 00:04:52.660
Cracked heels that are very painful, or ingrown toenails,

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:54.616
are better seen by a podiatrist.

00:04:55.043 --> 00:04:57.576
Write it in the internal notes in VaraaAi:

00:04:57.842 --> 00:05:02.056
how the skin was, the pressure the client likes, and the products used.

00:05:02.636 --> 00:05:04.942
There are a few very common mistakes.

00:05:05.045 --> 00:05:06.782
Soaking water that is too hot.

00:05:07.106 --> 00:05:08.542
Soaking too long.

00:05:08.885 --> 00:05:11.582
Filing the heel until the client feels it burn.

00:05:12.091 --> 00:05:14.542
Cutting into the living skin around the nails.

00:05:14.651 --> 00:05:16.782
Reusing the previous client's buffer.

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:19.182
And forgetting to dry between the toes:

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:22.942
damp skin between the toes is where fungus loves to grow.

00:05:23.368 --> 00:05:27.182
Avoid these mistakes, and the client will feel clean, and safe.

00:05:27.852 --> 00:05:28.876
Step fourteen:

00:05:29.063 --> 00:05:29.676
clean up.

00:05:29.933 --> 00:05:31.036
Throw away the liner.

00:05:31.224 --> 00:05:34.811
Clean the tub with soap and a brush, rinse it, then disinfect it,

00:05:34.761 --> 00:05:36.716
for the contact time on the bottle.

00:05:37.213 --> 00:05:38.156
Metal tools:

00:05:38.345 --> 00:05:40.156
clean them, then sterilize them.

00:05:40.425 --> 00:05:42.796
Towels go into a laundry basket with a lid.

00:05:43.048 --> 00:05:45.276
Wipe the chair, and wash your hands.

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:49.742
At the end of the day, clean more thoroughly, especially whirlpool tubs,

00:05:49.692 --> 00:05:51.356
as the manufacturer instructs.

00:05:51.584 --> 00:05:54.396
And now, please take the short quiz below the video.
